  "gaps": [
    "The capture labels units only as \"credits\"; it does not explicitly say semester hours. Semester was assumed.",
    "The program table lists only a combined block: \"Remaining General Education and Elective Courses 54.\" The 26 general-education / 28 elective split was derived, not printed. It assumes the 15 business-core credits that \"may be applied to general education requirements\" cover the following areas, inferred from the course sequencing table: WRTG 112 (communications), STAT 200 (mathematics 3), ECON 201/203 (behavioral and social sciences 6), and CIFS 300 (computing 3). Under that assumption, 41 total gen-ed credits minus 15 leaves 26 remaining, and 54 minus 26 leaves 28 for electives.",
    "Residency rules are not tied to specific courses: at least 30 credits (normally the final 30) must be completed at UMGC; half the credits within the major must be completed at UMGC; and at least 15 upper-level credits must be completed at UMGC. The capture does not say which of these courses must be taken at UMGC, so no requirement is flagged institutionalOnly.",
    "Grade rules: a minimum grade of C is required for courses applied to the major, and WRTG 112 must be completed with a C- or better within the first 24 credits. Separately, at least half of the major credits must come from graded coursework.",
    "Exact course options for each general-education block (e.g., the allowed disciplines for arts/humanities and sciences, and the PACE course list) are summarized in titles only. The full eligibility lists are in the capture text."
  ],
